1
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,980
The ultimate handsome

2
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:30,980
Leaping lightly over these hectic times

3
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:37,440
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,780
I wanna time is what I want

5
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:45,080
So I keep wearing nothing
but the latest trends

6
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,220
Because my natural face
wins them over instantly

7
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,980
Let it rain

8
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do.
Once I start running, my dreams never stop

9
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,240
Let's set sail for tomorrow too, yeah

10
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:10,800
Everybody can do.
Even if I stray a little, it doesn't hurt

11
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:17,820
Holding onto restless curiosity,
I kept aiming higher and stronger

12
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:30,880
I'll boost my win rate.

13
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,260
I'm broke.

14
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:40,900
Just 130 yen.

15
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:44,160
Damn, I thought I had at
least another 1,000 yen.

16
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:49,240
Do I really have to get
through a whole week on 130 yen?

17
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:53,520
You have to think carefully about how you spend your paycheck,
I've told you.

18
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:55,280
How many times do I have to say it,
Ryo-chan?

19
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:56,640
Wait.

20
00:01:58,040 --> 00:01:59,100
Please, Reiko-chan.

21
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:03,140
If I just have one katsudon, I'll drink water and
tough it out till the end of the month, I promise.

22
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:04,660
No.

23
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:08,980
Learn your lesson from this and start
keeping an allowance ledger next month.

24
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:13,380
Come on,
you could at least lend me a little bit.

25
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:16,920
I'm starving.

26
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:17,680
Aaaaaah.

27
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:20,280
There's nothing particular to eat.

28
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,160
I'll just watch some TV, I guess.

29
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:26,460
Juicy meat

30
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:32,100
Delicious.

31
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:34,660
Dokudoku, yeah!

32
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:36,520
That dokudoku is going to melt my stomach!

33
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,560
Damn it!

34
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,760
Eating meat right before payday,
you bastard!

35
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,200
I'll be at my best now!

36
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:43,440
Don't air shows like this, damn it!

37
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:45,900
I love you.

38
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:49,080
I really love you.

39
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,480
I really love you.

40
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,080
Really, really -

41
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,360
Really, really love you.

42
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:58,520
No wonder you only get 3%
making dramas like this.

43
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,440
Analio-chan

44
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:03,480
You certainly know a lot about ratings.

45
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:07,100
Knowing TV ratings is
common knowledge these days.

46
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,160
Yeah, yeah.

47
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:13,360
Mimi-chan gets a shampoo every week,
with a dog's sash on.

48
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,380
Her clothes are Hanel.

49
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:17,520
Her shoes are custom-made Heragamo.

50
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,840
Kobe beef is her favorite

51
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,580
Wow!

52
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:22,100
Nah!

53
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,660
How dare a dog!

54
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:32,160
Ryo-san, what are you doing?

55
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:33,520
I'm starving...

56
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:35,240
Are you hallucinating or something?

57
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,440
Let's hurry up and eat.

58
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:40,300
Ganyaraa!

59
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:41,400
Gaigai!

60
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:47,420
These days, TV doesn't understand
viewers' feelings one bit!

61
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:50,340
How infuriating!

62
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:55,520
Activities like this in
Tsurukame Prefecture...

63
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:59,680
Well, Reiko,
you saved some for me after all?

64
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,540
This is Kei-chan's.

65
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:05,660
Come on, don't be so uptight about it.

66
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:08,460
I told you, it's Kei-chan's!

67
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:11,160
Speaking of which,
Nakagawa's late, isn't he?

68
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,014
That's right.

69
00:04:12,064 --> 00:04:15,380
He should be back from patrol about now.

70
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:19,340
Tsurukame Prefecture's katsudon
loses half its flavor once it cools.

71
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,040
I'll eat it myself after all!

72
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:26,820
Ryo-chan! Eating other people's
things without permission is theft!

73
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:30,400
I-I-I don't mind!

74
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:32,540
Ryo-chan!

75
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,060
Ta-da!

76
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:41,860
Reiko, you're so stingy!
Come on, what's the harm in eating a little?

77
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:47,100
What are you doing?
I'm going inside, you know.

78
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,640
Hey, old man, watch yourself.

79
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:50,240
Old man?

80
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:56,460
What's that over there?

81
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,798
Nakagawa-san, Nakagawa-san,

82
00:04:58,848 --> 00:05:00,640
you haven't done anything at all,
Nakagawa-san.

83
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,660
Excuse me, I'm on duty.

84
00:05:02,660 --> 00:05:05,120
Please, make way for us.

85
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,780
Nakagawa, turn that way.

86
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:08,160
Nakagawa?

87
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:09,080
Stop it.

88
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,620
S-senpai.

89
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:14,060
Oh no, oh no,
what are you doing in a place like this?

90
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:16,600
Senpai, help me, please.

91
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:18,460
What on earth is this commotion?

92
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:19,780
I don't know.

93
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:23,580
Are you all right, Senpai?

94
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,120
N-Nakagawa!

95
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:30,620
Do something, anything!

96
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,500
Th-this way,
I can't move forward even one centimeter!

97
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,540
No, if you could break up that activity,
I'd be willing to help you!

98
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,780
Please!

99
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:38,920
Alright!

100
00:05:39,920 --> 00:06:04,220
!

101
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,780
Senpai, you came! I'm saved.

102
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,420
Just hurry up and put your foot down!

103
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:10,040
Understood.

104
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:19,780
Senpai, are you okay?

105
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,520
If you're going to stop,
at least say you're stopping.

106
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:24,760
Sorry, that microbus just suddenly -

107
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:31,460
I'm Sugihara, a producer at Kantō TV.

108
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,300
Kantō TV.

109
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:37,680
And I'm Yamamoto, the director, too!

110
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:40,340
So, what does Kantō TV want?

111
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,240
Well, you see...

112
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:47,100
We're doing a full-day exclusive
feature on Officer Nakagawa!

113
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:48,880
Okay.

114
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:51,240
A thorough, 24-hour follow-up!

115
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,880
Why me?

116
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:58,920
Here you go, this one.

117
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:00,540
It's Nakagawa.

118
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:03,660
The Nice Guy Contest I spotted around town.

119
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:06,340
Nakagawa-chan wins by a landslide.

120
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:09,520
This is what caused that commotion earlier.

121
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:16,400
Hello?

122
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,040
Nakagawa, did you go to Kantō TV?

123
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:23,220
Yes, but Chief, what exactly is this about?

124
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:25,800
If you'd appear on TV,

125
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,900
it'd really boost
Katsushika Station's image.

126
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,180
Please, do cooperate with them.

127
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:31,180
Chief, you can't be serious!

128
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:37,960
Look! They're back!
Nakagawa, let's do something about this!

129
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,360
So they just want to film my day, right?

130
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:43,060
Alright! Let's do it!

131
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:43,780
Yay!

132
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:45,680
Then please, follow me!

133
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:46,820
Yeah!

134
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:02,780
Young master, it's morning.

135
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:04,480
Good morning.

136
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:21,020
The uniform you ordered from
Burberry has arrived from England.

137
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:23,440
Yeah, I'll try it on when I get back.

138
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:34,040
Young master, have a good day.

139
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,096
Okay,

140
00:08:39,146 --> 00:08:42,480
That was great, Nakagawa.

141
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,720
I tried to recreate this
morning's atmosphere exactly.

142
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:50,120
Hey, with this we should
easily get a 20% rating, right?

143
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:52,720
It's as if you don't understand
what viewers feel at all.

144
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,880
A thorough 24-hour close-up.

145
00:08:55,880 --> 00:09:00,000
Lately we've been constantly
fighting for the worst ratings slot.

146
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:03,680
1.2%, 1.0%, 1.3%.

147
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,940
At this rate,
the show's cancellation is certain.

148
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:07,880
Move.

149
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,540
What could an amateur
like you possibly know?

150
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:12,800
It's the amateurs who watch the show.

151
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:18,740
The 24-hour all-out coverage of that old man's food stall,
years ago.

152
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:22,520
That one pulled in a 20%
audience rating, right?

153
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,040
That emotion we felt back then.

154
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:26,660
That old man's smile back then.

155
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:30,580
Even now,
it's burned into my mind and won't leave.

156
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:32,280
Ohhhh.

157
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:35,400
When it comes to 24-hour all-out coverage,

158
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:38,960
it was modest, but it stayed
true to ordinary people's lives,

159
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:42,500
and at one point it was even called
the flagship show of Kantō TV.

160
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,560
And now look at it.

161
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:47,300
Just showing Nakagawa's
rich-kid lifestyle as it is.

162
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:48,640
Okay, that's a wrap.

163
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:51,400
We can't keep doing the same thing forever.

164
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,340
Yeah, but it's still a flop

165
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,520
Ramen and gyoza

166
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:02,680
Welcome!

167
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:04,080
Get it?

168
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:07,800
You're about to serve spaghetti

169
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:10,500
to customers who just walked
under the ramen shop's noren.

170
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:13,020
Yes, that's right.

171
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,240
Exactly as you say.

172
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,820
S-Sugihara-san

173
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:22,000
What kind of show do viewers want right now?

174
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:22,960
W-wait a minute.

175
00:10:24,340 --> 00:10:27,380
A reunion show that
wrings tears from viewers.

176
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:29,100
Like what?

177
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:32,720
It's a contest of peeking at other people's misfortune,
using the reunion format as a pretext.

178
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,440
Meaning what?

179
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:35,640
Listen.

180
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:38,660
Viewers want to see
other people's misfortune.

181
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:41,680
We're going to satisfy that desire.

182
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:43,680
The program concept is...

183
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:46,480
Poverty

184
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:48,160
I see.

185
00:10:50,660 --> 00:10:54,020
Depending on the terms,
I can guarantee these high ratings.

186
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:58,020
Our crack director, Ryotsu,
will go all out for you.

187
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,640
It's a make-or-break gamble,
but let's do it.

188
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,580
But...

189
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:04,920
We'd really appreciate your wisdom,
Director Ryotsu.

190
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:09,680
Let's go with a performance-based deal:
100,000 yen per 1% of ratings.

191
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:12,340
100,000 yen per 1%.

192
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:15,800
I wonder what the senior is thinking.

193
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:21,260
Operation: Remake Nakagawa-chan
into a Thoroughly Ordinary Man

194
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:22,220
Cue!

195
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:37,680
Nakagawa will be set up
as living in the dormitory.

196
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:41,840
Nakagawa-kun, living cheerfully and
modestly in the single officers' dormitory.

197
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,060
Listen, Ryo-chan.

198
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,360
I think staging it would be bad, though.

199
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:47,540
Staging?

200
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:48,800
It is!

201
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,940
This isn't staging at all!

202
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:53,940
Then what exactly is it?

203
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:55,580
It's direction.

204
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:57,860
Direction, then.

205
00:11:57,860 --> 00:12:03,480
Mom, I'm back.

206
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:05,920
Ryo-san, you're back early.

207
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:06,680
Yeah, well.

208
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,560
Alright, the ending's starting,
come on, come on.

209
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:10,140
Is that a guest?

210
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:12,000
I'll put you on TV too, Mom.

211
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,380
TV?

212
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:17,360
Pardon the intrusion, we're sorry
to bother you while you're so busy.

213
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:30,720
Awful.

214
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,260
R-really,

215
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:35,600
it might give viewers a
sense of superiority here,

216
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:36,800
but

217
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:41,880
Do you really live here every day?

218
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:43,160
Of course I do.

219
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:46,060
Come on, come up to the ending sense.

220
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:47,880
I'll make some tea for you now.

221
00:12:48,380 --> 00:12:49,440
No, thank you.

222
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,200
Let's start with waking up.

223
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:55,420
Set up your shot from a low angle here.

224
00:12:57,640 --> 00:12:59,500
Give it a twist from above the head,

225
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:02,140
then BAM, right in the face.

226
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:04,800
Amateurs are such a pain.

227
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:07,680
A camera mark that
unnatural is a no-go, right?

228
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:09,700
Hey, Sugihara.

229
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:11,560
Y-yeah, well...

230
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,820
Director, shut up.

231
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:14,800
What?

232
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,960
Even a fresh fish gets ruined
when it lands with a lousy chef.

233
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,260
That's bad luck

234
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,520
Well, let's see it, then.

235
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:27,360
Are you going to sleep in this futon?

236
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,600
You can't exactly sleep in your uniform,
can you?

237
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,420
Hurry up and take off your jacket.

238
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:34,300
Those pajamas...

239
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:35,060
Pajamas?

240
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:36,180
Something like that.

241
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:37,580
Now that you mention it,

242
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:39,880
I'm sure it was this butt.

243
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:44,460
Well, that's the situation.

244
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:47,520
The common-folk officers are
on standby in their own shirts.

245
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:50,720
Is it like this?

246
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:53,140
Nope, that's not it.

247
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:54,640
Hey, Eddie.

248
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:57,700
You, you.

249
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:58,540
Me?

250
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,040
What did you say?

251
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:03,060
Yamamoto, just hold it in for now.

252
00:14:03,060 --> 00:14:04,480
Good? Shall we do it?

253
00:14:04,930 --> 00:14:07,240
Put that over there, and that over there.

254
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:09,300
Try swapping the stuff over
there with the stuff over here.

255
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:10,160
Okay!

256
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,680
No, no,
it's not just a matter of lining things up.

257
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,500
Nakagawa, try reaching out your hand.

258
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:23,680
Yes.

259
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:29,560
Everything is within arm's reach.

260
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:32,260
And a photo of a beautiful woman,
casually placed

261
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:38,460
Well, this is what realism is all about,
isn't it?

262
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,560
By the way, AD Yamamoto.

263
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,520
Y-yes!

264
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,680
Don't you think something's missing?

265
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:47,140
You're pathetic.

266
00:14:47,580 --> 00:14:48,980
Can't you even understand this much?

267
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,540
It's Katoributa.

268
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:55,040
Katoributa?

269
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:58,680
Go buy some Katoributa, hurry!

270
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:00,520
Fine, I'll go buy it.

271
00:15:01,380 --> 00:15:03,260
Katoributa in winter, senpai?

272
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,820
Nakagawa won't understand this, will he?

273
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,740
A summer wind chime at a winter windowsill,

274
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,320
a winter kotatsu at a
midsummer dining table.

275
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,300
That's the melancholy of a single man.

276
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:17,620
With this, we'll squeeze out housewives' tears,
nice and tight.

277
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:19,820
That staged footage...

278
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:23,900
I'd guess the ratings will go up about 3%.

279
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,180
Hahaha!

280
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:31,600
Your charm is really oozing out

281
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,280
Standby, OK!

282
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:40,700
I slept well!

283
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:43,020
Nice weather again today.

284
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:44,200
Cut!

285
00:15:44,700 --> 00:15:45,540
Why?

286
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:48,700
There's no everyman who looks this
put-together right after waking up.

287
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,400
Remember,
we haven't used any styling lotion.

288
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:58,480
We'll give him bed-head like this
with leftover oil from the frying pan.

289
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:02,820
Make his eyes red from a nightcap,
slightly puffy and swollen.

290
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,500
It's still lacking a
bit of that scruffiness.

291
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,360
Hey, Ryo-chan,
that's enough of that already.

292
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,120
Don't interfere with the direction.

293
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,360
For the finishing touch,
the wake-up fashion...

294
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,280
Due to budget constraints.

295
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:43,620
!

296
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:46,460
Wake-up tune!

297
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:53,320
Did you see that?
This is what a human's wake-up looks like!

298
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,400
Go on, try it.

299
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:55,120
Yes, sir!

300
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:04,400
No, no, no way.

301
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:10,620
You're still not a handsome,
wealthy man like me,

302
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:13,000
why would you have to
do something like this?

303
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:19,380
Right? Yes,
living standards for ordinary folk

304
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:23,780
are simply different, baby.
That insufferable pride

305
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:26,120
is showing. I didn't mean it like that.

306
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:30,800
You have to throw it away, Nakagawa. Your status
as the heir of the wealthy Nakagawa family,

307
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:36,040
your arrogance about being a handsome man,
throw it all away and become completely bare.

308
00:17:36,040 --> 00:17:39,000
Tough direction. Well, I give in.

309
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,920
Good morning.

310
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,420
Don't chill it again this morning.

311
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:54,840
Damn it.

312
00:17:54,840 --> 00:18:02,500
This stinks.

313
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:06,700
Why's there mold on it?

314
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:09,220
This one's bad.

315
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:11,500
Hehehehe.

316
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:15,259
Right, I wiped with this after eating ramen,
some time ago,

317
00:18:15,309 --> 00:18:17,800
so it just aged like that

318
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:20,640
Well, for another week or two...

319
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:22,840
Kaah!

320
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:24,880
Why can't we just leave it like this?

321
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,220
Sorry, senpai.

322
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:34,000
I can't fart.

323
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,440
Cart.

324
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:36,780
It's OK.

325
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:39,180
Well, setting your hair aside,

326
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:42,940
you've really broken free,
Nakagawa, as an ordinary man.

327
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:45,500
With this, a 5% rating is guaranteed.

328
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:49,280
Now it's just how much
viewer-pleasing material

329
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,980
we can cram in within the time.
It's a contest.

330
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:01,940
Officer Nakagawa,
the poor man of the people,

331
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:04,940
rummages through garbage
bins to save on food costs.

332
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:15,920
Kind Nakagawa shares the fried chicken
bento he found for his own dinner with a dog.

333
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:23,140
That captures the hearts of dog
lovers and boosts ratings by 1%!

334
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:30,620
Nakagawa is also a gentle older-brother
type of officer who loves children.

335
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:36,320
That wins over housewives and children,
boosting ratings by 1%!

336
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:45,000
At the Kameari Park police box, he has a
splendid superior, Senior Officer Ryotsu,

337
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:50,260
who sometimes treats
hungry Nakagawa to ramen.

338
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:51,340
Gaaah!

339
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:56,240
With the appearance of ramen that even gourmets rave about,
ratings shoot up 10%!

340
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:01,500
What's going on here, Ryo-chan?

341
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:02,020
No, that's wrong!

342
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:04,400
Yeah, but the camera's too high!

343
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:05,680
I'll shoot it myself!

344
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:13,180
Alright, Reiko!
Just keep walking straight ahead!

345
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:14,480
Come on!

346
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,000
Don't shoot so much from below, okay!

347
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,680
Nakagawa frames in right there.

348
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:21,700
Rain

349
00:20:21,700 --> 00:20:22,300
Yes.

350
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:28,860
A sexy beauty and a handsome
guy with a one-sided crush.

351
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:31,580
Roughly what percentage is this?

352
00:20:32,020 --> 00:20:35,060
Catching the Yumeji demographic,
we're at least 5 percent for sure.

353
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:36,400
What time is it?

354
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,580
It's four-thirty.

355
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:39,200
Alright, they'll be here any moment.

356
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:44,320
That's the auntie from Nikoniko Dormitory.

357
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:45,900
Go, Nakagawa!

358
00:21:32,700 --> 00:21:33,560
Four million!

359
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:37,060
Now, tearful Nakagawa

360
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:40,880
enters the public bathhouse.

361
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:48,320
Playful Nakagawa, who sometimes
mistakenly walks into the wrong bath.

362
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:51,140
Soap, soap...

363
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:52,640
Found it!

364
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:55,740
Shampoo!

365
00:21:57,560 --> 00:21:59,080
Lucky, there's some left!

366
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:03,800
Collecting and using the soap and shampoo people left behind,
that's what an everyman cop does.

367
00:22:05,540 --> 00:22:08,120
And to finish, a niche fruit milk.

368
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:10,280
Alright, now for the climax!

369
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:14,740
So that's how a day in the life
of everyman officer Nakagawa goes.

370
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:16,380
Mom...

371
00:22:16,380 --> 00:22:19,080
He's such a cheapskate,
cheapskate, cheapskate.

372
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:20,780
I missed you.

373
00:22:22,140 --> 00:22:23,320
Reiko-san...

374
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:33,380
Well done, Nakagawa.

375
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:36,540
You really became a
commoner through and through.

376
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:39,120
That's just too much.

377
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:40,760
Poor Kei-chan.

378
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:43,360
W-this is a different person.

379
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:44,680
That's not me.

380
00:22:45,560 --> 00:22:46,780
Nakagawa-chan.

381
00:22:47,330 --> 00:22:48,160
Ryo-chan.

382
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:51,500
So, as it turns out,

383
00:22:53,420 --> 00:22:56,380
letters and faxes of encouragement
addressed to Nakagawa-chan

384
00:22:56,380 --> 00:22:59,920
have been pouring in from all over the country,
filling the staff room with packages.

385
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:02,760
It's all thanks to Nakagawa's acting skills.

386
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:05,780
I-I've deceived the public.

387
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:08,400
How am I supposed to apologize for this?

388
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,420
Right.

389
00:23:10,160 --> 00:23:12,880
By the way,
what about the all-important ratings?

390
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,540
Get this, 30%!

391
00:23:14,540 --> 00:23:16,640
I see, so that means...

392
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:18,560
Hee-hoo-mee-hee.

393
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:21,040
My cut is three million yen, right?

394
00:23:21,820 --> 00:23:26,400
That's how it got exposed
that Ryo-chan was the director.

395
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:29,320
We don't need people who are
less capable than amateurs.

396
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:30,660
You two.

397
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:33,780
You're fired, so there's no money either.

398
00:23:33,780 --> 00:23:34,760
W-what?

399
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,540
Ryotsu!

400
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:39,220
C-Chief...

401
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:43,740
So you were behind that fake show,
after all?

402
00:23:43,740 --> 00:23:47,080
That was the crystallized sweat
and tears of Nakagawa and me.

403
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:48,440
Hey.

404
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,860
But Senpai forced me to!

405
00:23:51,360 --> 00:23:53,620
The Chief was pretty good, wasn't he?

406
00:23:53,620 --> 00:23:55,320
You're really something.

407
00:23:56,500 --> 00:23:57,540
You idiot...

408
00:24:05,100 --> 00:24:08,640
Who's this walking
designer catalog of a man?

409
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:11,340
He's the super-rich Reiji Shiratori,
you know.

410
00:24:11,340 --> 00:24:14,260
Did he fall for Reiko at first sight and
follow her all the way to the police box?

411
00:24:14,260 --> 00:24:17,480
Hey Reiko,
do something about this dangerous guy.

412
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:21,620
I'm the super-rich Reiji Shiratori.
Nice to meet you.

413
00:24:28,980 --> 00:24:32,680
Even if you try to stop the clock,

414
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps on passing.

415
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:42,720
So don't sulk with that frown,

416
00:24:44,300 --> 00:24:48,020
let's laugh it off and keep on living.

417
00:24:50,300 --> 00:24:57,920
Even if today is rainy,

418
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:03,440
tomorrow will be sunny.

419
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye.

420
00:25:22,300 --> 00:25:30,260
Good things will come.
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

